## Account Metrics

One account's revenue health, read from the invoices and subscriptions the host card passes in: MRR (active and trial subscriptions, yearly prices divided by 12), ARR, Outstanding (what is still owed on open invoices, tax included), Collected (paid invoices) and the count of overdue invoices. A new payment or subscription updates the strip without a reload.

```gts
import { AccountMetrics } from '@cardstack/catalog/matrix-app/crm/components/account-metrics';

<AccountMetrics
  @account={{@model.account}}
  @invoices={{this.invoices.instances}}
  @subscriptions={{this.subscriptions.instances}}
/>
```

The block runs no query of its own: it sums the invoices and subscriptions it is given, keeping only the ones linked to `@account`. Load them in the host card, for example with a search filtered on `account.id`, as the example does. The sums are in the account's currency (its subscriptions', else its invoices'); amounts in another currency are left out rather than added as if they were the same money.

### Example

Acme Industries, with its Workspace Pro and data add-on subscriptions and its invoices.

### Non-goals

Cross-account rollups such as pipeline value or win rate. Storing these numbers on any card.
